Cool.  If you can get unrestricted in long sword, frosty's one of the
best weapons in the game.  Until then, keep using mojo (it's the best
+0 weapon in the game for plain damage, though it destroys inventory).
The "blast you" thing does at most 40 damage w/o MR, or 20 with MR, so
it's not a huge deal if you're reasonably far along.  It'll only blast
you when you first get it into inventory (e.g. pick it up or take it
out of a bag), wield it, or invoke it.  It won't blast you at random.

Once you don't need Mojo, I'd stash it (e.g. in a container on
Elbereth) to avoid blowing up valuable rings/wands.  Frosty destroys
potions, which are generally less important (though some can be quite
valuable).

I don't know if it'll still blow up items if given to a pet, but I
assume it would in which case I'd much rather have it stashed than have
a pet using it.  The particular items that Mojo destroys make it by far
the worst of the "good" artifact weapons, and unless I'm in the very
early game I'd rather use Vorpal Sword, Sunsword, or Snickersnee than
Mojo.

You're not a valk, but for future reference it's never a good idea to
throw Mojo.  Brutal devteam trap.



